#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
sd_elements_scan.py — Deterministic SD Elements characteristic scanner.

Produces a schema-conformant {component}-sd-elements.json artifact by statically
scanning a source repository (and optionally a CD/deployment repository) for
literal code signals — annotations, dependency coordinates, config keys, file
patterns — as defined by an SD Elements add-on ruleset (Application Type,
Functional Attributes, Application Security Tier, Application Classification).

DESIGN GOALS
------------
1. Zero LLM calls in the core detection path. Every field is derived from a
   regex/manifest match against real repository content. This is intentional:
   the source ruleset is expressed entirely as literal tokens (annotations,
   dependency names, config keys), which is a static-analysis problem, not a
   reasoning problem. Determinism > fluency for a compliance artifact.
2. Zero organization-specific hardcoding. "Internal" package prefixes (e.g.
   your internal Maven groupId convention) are supplied at runtime via
   --internal-package-prefixes. Nothing about your org is embedded in this file.
3. No secrets on the command line. The GitHub token is read only from an
   environment variable and sent only as an Authorization header — never
   written into a clone URL, a log line, or a temp file.
4. No git binary dependency. Repository content is fetched via the GitHub
   REST API tarball endpoint using only the Python standard library.
5. Fail loud, not soft. Missing required inputs, unreachable repos, invalid
   tokens, or a JSON structure that doesn't validate against the target
   schema all raise a hard error with a specific message — nothing is
   silently defaulted or guessed.

KNOWN LIMITATION (stated, not hidden)
--------------------------------------
This is a regex + manifest-parser detection layer, not a full AST/code-graph
engine. It is deliberately scoped to be a self-contained, zero-dependency,
100%-reproducible alternative to an LLM call. For maximum precision (e.g.
distinguishing a *called* method from a *string literal* mentioning the same
name), wire an AST-based code-graph indexer in as an additional evidence
source and merge its hits into the same Hit model used here — the JSON
assembly, decision tables, and confidence scoring do not need to change.

USAGE
-----
    export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx            # never pass as a CLI argument
    python3 sd_elements_scan.py \
        --source-repo your-org/your-service \
        --component your-service \
        --app-id APP-1234 \
        --owner platform-engineering \
        --mnemonic your-app-bundle \
        --data-classification internal \
        [--cd-repo your-org/your-service-cd] \
        [--internal-package-prefixes com.yourorg,com.yourorg.internal] \
        [--output-dir ./out]

Only Python 3.9+ standard library is required. No pip installs.
"""

